      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "The analysis is complete. The answer file contains `0.99250`.\n\n**Summary of what was done:**\n\n1. **Extracted** PCE (Table 10, column 1 \"Total\") and PFI (Table 12, column 1 \"Total\") — annual values for 1973–2023, plus 2024 as the average of the three available quarters (PCE: 19,678.6; PFI: 5,201.1, in billions).\n2. **Deflated** each nominal series by the CPI (indexed 2024=1) to get real values.\n3. **Applied the HP filter** (λ = 100) to the natural log of each real series to extract the cyclical components.\n4. **Computed the Pearson correlation** between the two cyclical components: **0.992495664984462**.\n5. **Wrote** the result rounded to 5 decimal places to `workspace/answer.txt`: `0.99250`.\n\nThe very high correlation (~0.99) is expected: consumption and investment are both strongly procyclical, so their HP-detrended components move together almost in lockstep over the business cycle.",
      "text": "The analysis is complete. The answer file contains `0.99250`.\n\n**Summary of what was done:**\n\n1. **Extracted** PCE (Table 10, column 1 \"Total\") and PFI (Table 12, column 1 \"Total\") — annual values for 1973–2023, plus 2024 as the average of the three available quarters (PCE: 19,678.6; PFI: 5,201.1, in billions).\n2. **Deflated** each nominal series by the CPI (indexed 2024=1) to get real values.\n3. **Applied the HP filter** (λ = 100) to the natural log of each real series to extract the cyclical components.\n4. **Computed the Pearson correlation** between the two cyclical components: **0.992495664984462**.\n5. **Wrote** the result rounded to 5 decimal places to `workspace/answer.txt`: `0.99250`.\n\nThe very high correlation (~0.99) is expected: consumption and investment are both strongly procyclical, so their HP-detrended components move together almost in lockstep over the business cycle.",
